# 4. Fix ALL Invalid useEffect Implementations

Search the entire project for invalid patterns such as:

```javascript
useEffect(async () => {
    ...
}, []);
```

or:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  return someAsyncFunction();
}, []);
```

or any effect that accidentally returns a Promise.

Correct them using:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
    const fetchData = async () => {
        try {
            ...
        } catch (error) {
            ...
        }
    };

    fetchData();
}, []);
```

If cleanup is required:

```javascript
useEffect(() => {
    let isMounted = true;

    const fetchData = async () => {
        try {
            const response = await ...

            if (isMounted) {
                ...
            }
        } catch (error) {
            if (isMounted) {
                ...
            }
        }
    };

    fetchData();

    return () => {
        isMounted = false;
    };
}, []);
```

Use the appropriate cleanup mechanism when required.

Do not blindly add `isMounted` everywhere if it is unnecessary.

Also fix:

```text
destroy is not a function
```

by identifying the actual invalid effect/cleanup causing it.

Search the entire project, not just the currently visible page.

After fixing, verify there are no remaining React `useEffect` warnings.

